.Dd 2026-05-30
.Dt NOMAD-INSTALL 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nomad-install
.Nd install or repair the full Project NOMAD stack
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm nomad install
.Op Fl -data-root Ar PATH
.Op Fl -tier Ar TIER
.Op Fl -models Ar names
.Op Fl -no-models
.Op Fl -yes
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm nomad install
brings up the complete Project NOMAD stack on this Mac: it installs the
required tools (Homebrew, OrbStack, native Ollama), provisions the data root,
starts the container stack, runs database migrations, seeds the services
catalog, and pulls the local AI models.
.Pp
The command is idempotent. Running it on a machine that already has NOMAD
installed repairs the stack in place rather than starting over, so it is also
the supported repair path after an interrupted install or a configuration
drift. When it finishes it prints the admin URLs and a count of the models
that were pulled.
.Pp
By default the command opens an interactive model picker so you can see which
models will be pulled and choose a different tier before any heavy work
begins. Passing any of
.Fl -tier ,
.Fl -models ,
.Fl -no-models ,
or
.Fl -yes
declares your intent up front and skips the picker.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -data-root Ar PATH
Use
.Ar PATH
as the data root for models, databases, and stored content. When omitted on a
fresh install the command prompts for a location; an existing data root is
reused without prompting.
.It Fl -tier Ar TIER
Select the model tier to pull. One of
.Cm auto ,
.Cm tiny ,
.Cm small ,
.Cm medium ,
.Cm large ,
.Cm xl ,
or
.Cm dreamy .
The default,
.Cm auto ,
sizes the model set to this Mac's hardware. Choosing a tier larger than the
auto-detected one triggers a warning before the pull commits.
.It Fl -models Ar names
Pull an explicit, space-separated list of model names instead of a tier. This
takes precedence over
.Fl -tier .
.It Fl -no-models
Install and start the stack but skip pulling any AI models. Useful when you
want the stack running before downloading models, or intend to pull them later
with
.Ic nomad models pull .
.It Fl -yes , Fl y
Assume yes to confirmation prompts and run non-interactively.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic nomad install
Interactive install with the model picker and hardware-sized model tier.
.It Ic nomad install --data-root /Volumes/NOMAD --tier medium --yes
Install onto an external drive, pull the medium model tier, and answer all
prompts automatically.
.It Ic nomad install --no-models
Bring up the stack now and defer model downloads.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr nomad 1 ,
.Xr nomad-reinstall 1 ,
.Xr nomad-uninstall 1 ,
.Xr nomad-up 1
